        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.438,
            0.724,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In all the above situations, the nature and the identity of the initial substance have somewhat changed. We have already learnt about physical and chemical changes of matter in our previous classes. Whenever a chemical change occurs, we can say that a chemical reaction has taken place.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.506,
            0.723,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may perhaps be wondering as to what is actually meant by a chemical reaction. How do we come to know that a chemical reaction has taken place? Let us perform some activities to find the answer to these questions.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.593,
            0.294,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 1.1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.572,
            0.373,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
